{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1776374850,"nonce":"rDoXHVSzUXd5x0uK1Js/l1RCiPk=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM7_Bc4vzrLzTEs"},"target":"8e8a7744cf467c18cff8331f0c639e593ae1a0e53fc73892b76f02144f26fd94","message":"## Problem\n\n`bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_baseline.param` describes\nbattery hardware that doesn't exist on BizzyBoat and a capacity far\nbelow the actual pack. The resulting telemetry is wrong in ways that\nwould matter if anything ever trusted `sensor_msgs/BatteryState.percentage`.\n\n(BizzyBoat and IzzyBoat happen to carry **identical** `BATT_*` values\ntoday, but the two boats have different batteries so the values can't\nbe correct for both. Origin and direction of any historical copying\nis unknown — they may have both been shipped from the factory this way.)\n\n## Evidence\n\n**From 2026-04-16 field test bags** (`~/data/logs/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-16T*`):\n\n| Session | Voltage range | Current | % at start | % at end |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 12:52 (4.5 h driving) | 26.09–28.39 V | 160 369 samples, **all ≈ 0 A** | 0.99 | 0.99 |\n| 17:20 (active hover) | 26.21–27.77 V | 18 247 samples, **all 0.000 A** | 0.99 | 0.99 |\n| 17:56 (active ops) | 26.16–27.66 V | 8 951 samples, **99.8% exactly 0 A** | 0.99 | 0.99 |\n\nVoltage reads correctly. Current reads exactly zero across 4.5 hours\nof thruster activity — there is no current sensor wired on BizzyBoat.\n`percentage` is stuck at 0.99 because ArduPilot computes it from\nintegrated `consumed_mAh`, which can't accumulate when current is zero.\n\n**From the EchoBoat 240 manual** (`~/bizzyboat/EchoBoat_240_Manual_V.pdf`):\n\n- §1.3 p. 3: \"Power 24 VDC\", \"Battery Endurance 9 hours at Survey Speed\"\n- §2.1 p. 5: batteries are **Torqeedo Power 24-3500**\n- §3.6.1 p. 25, Table 6:\n  - Rated voltage 25.64 V, final charging 29.05 V, final discharging 21 V\n  - Usable energy **3500 Wh** per pack, max discharge 180 A\n- §7.4.3 p. 81: \"Power 24-3500 should be stored between 22.6–24.2 VDC (never drop below)\"\n- BizzyBoat = EchoBoat 240 carries **2× Torqeedo Power 24-3500** in\n  parallel → 7000 Wh usable, ~273 Ah at 25.64 V.\n\nIzzyBoat = EchoBoat 160 with 4× different/smaller batteries (different\nmodel; not yet characterized) — out of scope for this issue.\n\n## Why the shipped params are wrong for BizzyBoat\n\n| Param | Current | Problem on BizzyBoat |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `BATT_MONITOR` | 4 | Claims analog voltage + current, but no current sensor is wired |\n| `BATT_CAPACITY` | 16000 mAh | ~16× too small for BizzyBoat's true ~273 000 mAh |\n| `BATT_CURR_PIN` | 15 | Points at an unconnected ADC — drifts around zero |\n| `BATT_LOW_VOLT` | 0 | No low-voltage warning threshold |\n| `BATT_CRT_VOLT` | 0 | No critical-voltage threshold |\n\n## Proposed change\n\nAdd BizzyBoat-specific overrides to `bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param`\n(leaving the factory baseline file untouched, consistent with existing\nGPS/IMU override pattern):\n\n```\nBATT_MONITOR     3             # voltage only (was 4: voltage + current)\nBATT_CAPACITY    273000        # 2× Torqeedo 24-3500 (was 16000)\nBATT_CURR_PIN    -1            # disable unconnected ADC (was 15)\nBATT_LOW_VOLT    22.5          # above mfr storage floor 22.6 V (was 0)\nBATT_CRT_VOLT    21.5          # just above mfr minimum 21.0 V (was 0)\n```\n\nKeep `BATT_VOLT_MULT=12.02` (voltage reads correctly per bag evidence).\nKeep `BATT_FS_{LOW,CRT}_ACT=0` — the ROS stack owns autonomy decisions,\nFCU-side failsafes stay off.\n\nAlso add `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_hardware.md` documenting\nthe battery pack, voltage thresholds, and the fact that no current\nsensor is wired (mirroring `docs/izzyboat_hardware.md`).\n\n## Expected outcome\n\n- `sensor_msgs/BatteryState.percentage` returns NaN instead of a\n  misleading stuck 0.99 — honest.\n- `mavros: Battery` diagnostic flips to WARN at 22.5 V and ERROR at\n  21.5 V, driving the annunciator audibly before damage threshold.\n- `BATT_CAPACITY` documents actual hardware for future use once a\n  current sensor is added (or Torqeedo BMS telemetry is integrated).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- IzzyBoat params — the two boats may need to diverge; IzzyBoat's pack\n  needs to be characterized before changing its params. Tracked\n  separately.\n- Wiring a current sensor (hardware change).\n- Reading Torqeedo BMS telemetry (would need custom integration — the\n  packs have an internal BMS but no standard CAN output).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `claude-opus-4-6[1m]`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1776374069,"nonce":"UR+vfX1ckzX6qD8xcfvPtm2Wc3Y=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM7_Bc4vzwAAAAW5URCF"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1776374069,"nonce":"OgOHu7gktXCbHtvLd+ShEuf7jg4=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM7_Bc4vzwAAAAW5URDR"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1777387636,"nonce":"ANeH/9BXkvYtgmcrpt+NqGY49B4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAnfrFA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/55#issuecomment-4336380692"},"message":"## Adding scope: SOC reporting also broken with current params\n\nSurfaced from [2026-04-27 deployment debrief](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/jazzy/docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md) — folding into this existing issue rather than opening a new one because the fix is in the same FCU param block PR #56 already touches.\n\n### What we observed\n\n`/bizzy/mavros/battery.percentage` reported **99% all day** (5+ hours of operation, including range test peaks) while the actual SOC dropped roughly 50-60%.\n\n### Three reasons it's wrong\n\n1. **No current sensor wired** between the Torqeedo packs and the Cube → BATT_MONITOR=4 has nothing to coulomb-count, so percentage is voltage-only.\n2. **LiFePO4 voltage is famously flat** from ~30-90% SOC. Pack went 28.98 V (start) → 27.60 V (end) while real SOC dropped 50-60%; voltage reveals basically nothing across this range.\n3. **ArduPilot's voltage→percentage map is calibrated for typical Li-ion-ish chemistries**, not LiFePO4.\n\n### What to add to the param rework\n\nTwo viable paths, pick one:\n\n- **(a) Disable the SOC report** (`BATT_CAPACITY = 0` or equivalent): the operator UI suppresses the percentage rather than showing a misleading 99%. Honest, simple.\n- **(b) Custom voltage→percentage map for LiFePO4 8S** with `BATT_FS_VOLTSRC`/related params: harder to calibrate, still inaccurate during use because of the flat-V curve, but at least nominally correct.\n\n(a) is the lower-risk option and likely the right call until a real current sensor lands.\n\n### Bag evidence\n\nCoulomb counting from PWM time-series gave **33-48% remaining at end of day** (linear vs quadratic models bound the answer). Voltage-based reading saying 99% is what the operator actually saw on the UI today.\n\nFull analysis: [dev log § \"Voltage / PWM / SOC analysis\"](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/jazzy/docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md).\n\n### Acceptance addition for PR #56\n\n- [ ] FCU param change so `/bizzy/mavros/battery.percentage` either reports nothing (recommended) or a LiFePO4-aware estimate, rather than the misleading constant-99% reading.\n\ncc @rolker — wanted to flag this is now in scope before the field-apply window.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1777410685,"nonce":"OugwxTTHKpX1DJHUxdm1mEBwSO0=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM7_Bc4vzwAAAAXQE33f"},"status":2}]}